{"step_index":162,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:32:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T20:02:55+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T20:02:55+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 289\n1: # 🔍 FraudLens AI\n2: ### *Detect smarter. Explain every alert. Reduce false alarms.*\n3: \n4: > **Zeckathon PS2 — Explainable Financial Risk & Fraud Analytics**\n5: \n6: FraudLens AI is a complete, locally-runnable prototype that combines a genuine ML prediction pipeline, three-outcome triage, interactive graph analysis, chronological replay, and a full investigator workflow — all built without paid APIs or bank credentials.\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## ✅ Quick Start (Windows / VS Code)\n11: \n12: ### Prerequisites\n13: - Python 3.12 ([download](https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3120/))\n14: - Node.js 20+ with npm ([download](https://nodejs.org/))\n15: \n16: ### Step 1 — Clone / Open the Project\n17: \n18: ```powershell\n19: # Open a new PowerShell terminal in VS Code\n20: cd \"C:\\path\\to\\fraudlens-ai\"\n21: ```\n22: \n23: ### Step 2 — Backend Setup\n24: \n25: ```powershell\n26: # Install Python dependencies\n27: pip install -r requirements.txt\n28: \n29: # Start the backend API server (from project root)\n30: cd backend\n31: python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload\n32: ```\n33: \n34: Backend will be available at: http://127.0.0.1:8000  \n35: Swagger API docs at: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs\n36: \n37: ### Step 3 — Frontend (Development Mode)\n38: \n39: Open a second terminal:\n40: \n41: ```powershell\n42: cd frontend\n43: npm install\n44: npm run dev\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Frontend will be available at: http://localhost:5173\n48: \n49: ### Step 4 — Frontend (Production Build — Served by Backend)\n50: "}
{"step_index":163,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:32:55Z","input_tokens":2849,"cache_read_tokens":107509,"output_tokens":386,"tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\README.md","Replacement":"---\n\n## 🚀 Deploying to Vercel\n\nFraudLens AI is pre-configured for **1-click unified Vercel deployment** hosting both the React/TypeScript frontend (via edge CDN) and the Python FastAPI prediction engine (via Vercel Serverless Functions).\n\n### Method 1: Git Integration (Recommended — Zero Setup)\n\n1. Push this directory to your GitHub / GitLab repository.\n2. Go to [vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new).\n3. Import your repository.\n4. Leave all build settings at default (`vercel.json` and root `package.json` automatically configure build, output directory, and serverless runtime).\n5. Click **Deploy**.\n\nVercel will build the frontend into `frontend/dist` and mount the Python FastAPI backend on `/api/*` automatically!\n\n### Method 2: Vercel CLI\n\n```bash\n# Install Vercel CLI if not already installed\nnpm i -g vercel\n\n# From the fraudlens-ai project root:\nvercel\n```\n\nFollow the prompts:\n- Set up and deploy? **Y**\n- Which scope? **Select your account**\n- Link to existing project? **N**\n- Project name: **fraudlens-ai**\n- Directory: **./**\n- Want to modify settings? **N** (settings are pre-configured in `vercel.json`)\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Project Structure","Target":"---\n\n## 📁 Project Structure"}}]}
{"step_index":164,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:33:02Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T20:03:02+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T20:03:02+05:30\nMade 1 replacement in C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\README.md starting at line 108 (+34/-0 lines)."}
{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:33:02Z","input_tokens":2546,"cache_read_tokens":108316,"output_tokens":1290,"tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# 🚀 FraudLens AI — Vercel Deployment Guide\n\nFraudLens AI is designed for seamless, full-stack serverless deployment on [Vercel](https://vercel.com). Both the React Vite frontend and the Python FastAPI prediction engine run from a single repository under a unified domain.\n\n---\n\n## 🏗️ Architecture on Vercel\n\n```\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                         │       Incoming HTTPS Traffic              │\n                         │    https://fraudlens-ai.vercel.app        │\n                         └─────────────────────┬─────────────────────┘\n                                               │\n                       ┌───────────────────────┴──────────────────────┐\n                       │                                              │\n              Paths: /api/*, /docs, /openapi.json             All other paths (/*)\n                       │                                              │\n                       ▼                                              ▼\n        ┌─────────────────────────────┐               ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n        │   Vercel Serverless Function│               │      Vercel Edge CDN        │\n        │       Python 3.12 Runtime   │               │     Static SPA Assets       │\n        │        `api/index.py`       │               │      `frontend/dist/`       │\n        │  (FastAPI Prediction Engine)│               │  (React + Tailwind + Vite)  │\n        └──────────────┬──────────────┘               └─────────────────────────────┘\n                       │\n       ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐\n       ▼                               ▼\n┌──────────────┐              ┌────────────────┐\n│ Model Store  │              │ Ephemeral DB   │\n│ 170KB Model  │              │ /tmp/fraudlens.db│\n│  (Read-only) │              │ (Self-healing  │\n└──────────────┘              │  Auto-seeding) │\n                              └────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Deployment Methods\n\n### Option A: Via GitHub (Recommended)\n\n1. **Push your code to GitHub**:\n   ```bash\n   git init\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"feat: FraudLens AI initial release\"\n   git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/fraudlens-ai.git\n   git branch -M main\n   git push -u origin main\n   ```\n\n2. **Connect to Vercel**:\n   - Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) and log in.\n   - Click **Add New...** → **Project**.\n   - Select your `fraudlens-ai` repository and click **Import**.\n   - **Framework Preset**: Leave as *Other* (configured by `vercel.json`).\n   - **Root Directory**: `./` (leave default).\n   - Click **Deploy**.\n\n---\n\n### Option B: Via Vercel CLI\n\nIf you have Node.js and npm installed:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install Vercel CLI\nnpm install -g vercel\n\n# 2. Login to Vercel\nvercel login\n\n# 3. Deploy from the project root\nvercel\n\n# 4. Deploy to Production\nvercel --prod\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Key Serverless Enhancements Made\n\n| Feature | How It Works in Serverless |\n|---------|----------------------------|\n| **Unified Routing** | `vercel.json` routes `/api/(.*)` to `api/index.py` and static requests to `frontend/dist`. |\n| **Model Ingestion** | The 170KB trained Scikit-learn champion model (`model_store/fraudlens_predictor.joblib`) is included in the serverless bundle via `includeFiles`. |\n| **Serverless SQLite** | Vercel provides a read-only filesystem except for `/tmp`. `backend/app/db/repository.py` automatically clones the pre-seeded SQLite database into `/tmp/fraudlens.db` upon function execution, ensuring full read/write support for feedback, uploads, and simulation without crashes. |\n| **Cold Start Auto-Seeding** | If a fresh serverless instance spins up with an empty `/tmp` database, `backend/app/api/endpoints.py` detects 0 transactions and automatically seeds the 2,480 benchmark transactions and demo cases from `data/synthetic_transactions.csv`. |\n| **API Client Dynamic Base URL** | `frontend/src/services/api.ts` automatically defaults to `/api` (same-origin), avoiding CORS or hardcoded hostnames, while honoring optional `VITE_API_URL` overrides. |\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Verification After Deployment\n\nOnce deployed, verify these endpoints:\n\n1. **Frontend**: Open `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/`\n2. **Swagger Docs**: Open `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/docs`\n3. **Health Check**: Open `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/api/health`\n   Expected response:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"status\": \"healthy\",\n     \"service\": \"FraudLens AI Prediction Engine\",\n     \"model_version\": \"v1.2.0-champion\",\n     \"database\": \"SQLite (Active)\",\n     \"synthetic_demo_badge\": true\n   }\n   ```\n4. **Interactive Demo**:\n   - Click **Case A** on the dashboard to view the legitimate luxury transaction.\n   - Click **Case B** to inspect the account takeover replay and counterfactual simulator.\n   - Click **Case C** to view the Cytoscape.js syndicate network radar.\n","Path":"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md"}}]}
