{"step_index":169,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:33:28Z","input_tokens":2316,"cache_read_tokens":110185,"output_tokens":970,"content":"### 🚀 Vercel Deployment Configuration Complete\n\nThe **FraudLens AI** codebase has been configured for a unified, full-stack serverless deployment on **Vercel** (both the React/TypeScript frontend and the Python FastAPI ML prediction engine under a single domain).\n\n---\n\n### 📦 Key Deployment Enhancements Added\n\n1. **Vercel Serverless Function Entrypoint (`api/index.py`)**\n   - Configured FastAPI ASGI adapter pointing to the production application.\n   - Tested and verified Python imports (`api.index.app` loads cleanly).\n\n2. **Serverless Production Requirements (`api/requirements.txt`)**\n   - Stripped dev/testing libraries (`pytest`, etc.) to keep the serverless bundle lightweight and fast to deploy.\n\n3. **Vercel Orchestration Config (`vercel.json`)**\n   - Automatic static frontend routing from `frontend/dist`.\n   - Automatic serverless function rewrites for `/api/*`, `/docs`, and `/openapi.json` to `api/index.py`.\n   - Bundles the 170KB trained model (`model_store/`) and data assets (`data/`) into the function image.\n\n4. **Self-Healing SQLite in Read-Only Serverless (`backend/app/db/repository.py`)**\n   - Vercel's serverless filesystem is read-only except for `/tmp`.\n   - On cold start, the database manager automatically mirrors the benchmark SQLite database to `/tmp/fraudlens.db`, ensuring all investigator actions (feedback, overrides, CSV scoring, live simulation) work smoothly without permission errors.\n\n5. **Cold-Start Auto-Seeding (`backend/app/api/endpoints.py`)**\n   - If a new serverless container boots without an existing database file, it auto-detects zero records and seeds the 2,480 benchmark transactions and demo cases from `data/synthetic_transactions.csv`.\n\n6. **Unified API Base URL (`frontend/src/services/api.ts`)**\n   - Client requests default to `/api` (same-origin), eliminating CORS or manual host configuration. Supports `VITE_API_URL` override if hosted separately.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 How to Deploy to Vercel\n\n#### Option 1: Via GitHub / GitLab (Recommended — Zero Config)\n\n1. Push the `fraudlens-ai` folder to your GitHub repository:\n   ```bash\n   git init\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"feat: FraudLens AI initial release\"\n   git branch -M main\n   git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/fraudlens-ai.git\n   git push -u origin main\n   ```\n2. Navigate to [vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new).\n3. Import your **`fraudlens-ai`** repository.\n4. Leave all settings at default (`vercel.json` handles the build command, output directory, and Python function routing).\n5. Click **Deploy**.\n\n#### Option 2: Via Vercel CLI\n\nFrom your terminal in the `fraudlens-ai` root folder:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install Vercel CLI (if not already installed)\nnpm install -g vercel\n\n# 2. Login & Deploy\nvercel\n\n# 3. Deploy to production\nvercel --prod\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Verification Checklist After Deploy\n\nOnce your Vercel deployment finishes:\n\n| URL Path | Expected Output |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/` | Full React dashboard with 3-minute demo cases, queue, replay lab, and graph radar |\n| `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/api/health` | `{\"status\": \"healthy\", \"service\": \"FraudLens AI Prediction Engine\", ...}` |\n| `https://<your-project>.vercel.app/docs` | Interactive Swagger API documentation |\n\nSee [`VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md`](file:///C:/Users/S%20Nandhakumar/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/fraudlens-ai/VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md) in the project directory for architecture diagrams and troubleshooting steps."}
